{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Af</b> — the Yerushalmi said that the bet is missing, and the meaning is <b>af zenachta</b> (surely You have rejected). But this is not correct, for it would not have been attached as in <b>af YHWH</b>; and if it were as he says, the alef would have a kamatz. Rather, it is like <b>gam</b> (also): You saved us in former days, and put our enemies to shame; and now not only have You not saved us, but You have even abandoned us. <b>vatkhalemeinu</b> — corresponding to <b>boshet</b> (shame)." "<b>vatkhalemeinu</b> — corresponding to the putting to shame."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:44.865935301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}